WEBVTT

01:42.010 --> 01:43.500
Good morning, Ken-chan.

02:01.710 --> 02:06.340
100 Loans and 100 Debts

02:32.910 --> 02:35.610
Onii-chan is... Onii-chan is...

02:38.260 --> 02:40.770
Hmm, what should I do?

02:47.210 --> 02:52.220
But... You can't always think, "That's fine."

02:53.310 --> 02:57.560
(Note: The sign says "Congratulations on coming back." and the watermelon says: "Nanami, this is for you.")

03:12.610 --> 03:19.350
That's not good. What should I do? What should I do?

03:20.410 --> 03:22.030
What should I do, Ken-chan?

03:27.510 --> 03:30.150
Hmm, summer vacation is finally over.

03:30.610 --> 03:34.620
I don't have to ask about it. Once I check what you've done over the summer, I'll know how you spent the summer vacation.

03:36.010 --> 03:38.040
Well, even though these hot days will continue for a while,

03:38.410 --> 03:41.780
You guys shouldn't give up.
Keep working and get over the summer.

03:45.790 --> 03:51.010
Here you go, this is the pumpkin pudding you mentioned last time.

03:53.110 --> 03:56.770
If you don't eat it fast, I'll take yours away.

04:05.710 --> 04:08.900
The pudding... will get warm...

04:13.410 --> 04:16.010
Come on, I'll make it for you again.

04:16.410 --> 04:17.800
Now you owe me another favor.

05:03.910 --> 05:05.490
Good morning.

05:06.260 --> 05:07.660
Ah, good morning.

05:07.800 --> 05:09.310
Hey, did you finish your homework?

05:18.310 --> 05:21.650
Ken-chan, I got two movie tickets.

05:22.010 --> 05:25.230
Let's go together. Two people going to a movie...

05:26.010 --> 05:27.650
isn't that a date?

05:28.210 --> 05:34.390
We can have some popcorn, but there's too much fizz in the cola. I guess I'll get some orange juice instead.

05:34.910 --> 05:36.150
Ken-chan, you'll have to drink cola.

05:37.310 --> 05:40.290
These tickets will be good until next week,
let's hurry up and go.

05:43.310 --> 05:45.270
This will be one favor you'll owe me too.

06:22.010 --> 06:24.620
It's getting cold, I'll close the window.

06:29.610 --> 06:31.150
It's already fall.

06:34.510 --> 06:37.980
Ken-chan, the season for yams has started.

06:38.310 --> 06:39.960
Let's go and harvest together.

06:44.010 --> 06:46.940
But this year's yield won't be that good.

06:47.410 --> 06:49.750
That's because I slacked off on the field work.

06:50.410 --> 06:52.290
This is one favor I owe you.

07:51.010 --> 07:56.670
They say this year will be colder than last year.
Maybe we'll get some snow.

07:58.050 --> 08:00.990
If it snows, how about we make a snowman?

08:01.510 --> 08:05.180
It hasn't snowed for several years.

08:05.560 --> 08:10.040
Oh yeah, I wanted to spend Christmas together with you.

08:11.090 --> 08:13.240
If it's possible, I want to spend it with just you.

08:15.910 --> 08:16.890
I was kidding!

08:27.810 --> 08:29.010
Suzuka-chan.

08:29.910 --> 08:31.500
Are those Ken-chan's clothes?

08:33.010 --> 08:36.710
He hasn't awakened yet, but his body seems fine.

08:40.010 --> 08:41.450
What should I do?

08:48.510 --> 08:49.760
Thank you very much.

09:00.430 --> 09:02.800
The snow stopped.

09:07.310 --> 09:10.060
But there's a bit on the ground.

09:12.410 --> 09:15.790
It looks like we'll still be able to make a small snowman.

09:16.310 --> 09:19.120
Ken-chan, let's make a snowman together.

09:23.710 --> 09:25.080
You owe me another favor now.

09:29.910 --> 09:32.280
Now you owe me a hundred favors, Ken-chan...

09:36.010 --> 09:39.530
You have to grant me one wish, okay?

09:40.710 --> 09:42.050
That's because you owe me a wish.

09:45.510 --> 09:49.010
Wake up, this is an order...

09:51.510 --> 09:56.860
Hey, Ken-chan, it's already the 100th favor... this is an order.

10:02.310 --> 10:06.750
Wake up, Ken-chan, you must wake up.

10:12.410 --> 10:13.650
Wake up...

10:14.410 --> 10:19.590
I don't know what to do when you're not with me.

10:22.410 --> 10:26.760
It's impossible... I'm not with you...

11:04.410 --> 11:07.530
I'm sure everybody thinks I'm the charming college student.

11:07.910 --> 11:10.380
I won't let anybody treat me like a little kid.

11:15.510 --> 11:16.730
Wait, Miss.

11:17.710 --> 11:18.520
W-What?

11:22.810 --> 11:26.090
No way. Junior high students aren't allowed.

11:26.310 --> 11:28.060
Jun...? I am...

11:28.210 --> 11:30.680
Geez, you're even dressed up.

11:30.710 --> 11:32.810
Let me finish.

11:43.110 --> 11:44.900
Tae-chan, don't push yourself so hard.

11:45.410 --> 11:46.490
I'm fine.

11:47.910 --> 11:48.870
T-Tae-chan?

11:51.710 --> 11:52.910
Sorry.

11:53.410 --> 11:54.420
Did you get hurt?

11:54.610 --> 11:55.310
No.

11:58.310 --> 12:00.550
Hiromi, did you get up yet?

12:00.910 --> 12:02.660
You'll be late.

12:04.810 --> 12:06.250
Hurry up.

12:07.910 --> 12:09.840
Yeah, I'm coming.

12:18.910 --> 12:23.290
Carrots, strawberries, and tomatoes.

12:48.810 --> 12:49.730
Nanami-chan.

12:58.310 --> 12:59.910
Good morning, Nanami-chan.

13:05.610 --> 13:07.010
Nanami onee-chan.

13:07.310 --> 13:09.850
We're in the same class now, Suzuka-chan.

13:10.210 --> 13:13.150
Yeah. Your hair?

13:13.510 --> 13:15.970
I cut it, since it's spring.

13:27.110 --> 13:28.150
Hello.

13:28.310 --> 13:29.490
Hello.

13:36.610 --> 13:39.650
Today I went to school.

13:39.810 --> 13:43.520
But I have to retake second year.

13:47.210 --> 13:51.110
But, Ken-chan, you're in second year too.

13:51.810 --> 13:56.980
It's the first time we'll be in the same class as Suzuka-chan.

13:58.710 --> 14:01.900
Hurry and wake up. I won't cry anymore.

14:05.210 --> 14:06.140
I was joking.

15:05.510 --> 15:06.930
Yo, you two.

15:07.110 --> 15:10.550
Hikari-chan, it's already the time when you visit.

15:10.610 --> 15:14.320
Yeah, it's summer already. Your hair?

15:14.610 --> 15:16.720
Yeah, I cut it.

15:17.610 --> 15:21.070
I didn't mean that. I meant, where's that fish hairpin?

15:22.210 --> 15:23.470
Well...

15:29.810 --> 15:34.040
Since it found a good friend, it'd be good to turn them into a wind chime.

15:42.310 --> 15:43.850
That's just like you.

15:47.810 --> 15:52.890
But, well, how long are you going to continue like this?

15:53.910 --> 15:58.660
How long? Perhaps I can't even answer that myself.

16:00.790 --> 16:01.770
Nanami...

16:02.410 --> 16:08.090
But I have no choice, since we're... that way...

16:20.010 --> 16:20.920
Hikari-chan.

16:21.210 --> 16:22.830
Did you see Nanami onee-chan?

16:24.210 --> 16:28.510
Geez, those two people... I have no choice.

16:32.810 --> 16:36.570
I have no choice, since we're "that" way already.

16:42.710 --> 16:44.820
I want you to tell me clearly.

16:45.710 --> 16:47.190
What is "that"?

16:47.410 --> 16:50.870
Well... is that the wish to be asked after a hundred favors?

16:51.110 --> 16:54.270
Yeah, tell me.

16:57.110 --> 16:58.260
Ken-chan?

17:00.610 --> 17:02.500
Since I like you...

17:07.570 --> 17:16.030
Well... I... like...

17:28.210 --> 17:29.430
I was joking.

17:31.110 --> 17:33.340
I was kidding, isn't that obvious?

17:33.810 --> 17:37.210
I was kidding too.

17:43.810 --> 17:52.700
I lied. That, "I was kidding," I lied to you...

17:53.510 --> 17:55.920
I like you, I love you.

18:07.310 --> 18:12.060
The wind is strong, I'll close the window a little bit.

18:31.110 --> 18:32.050
What a beautiful sound.

18:41.710 --> 18:42.790
Ken-chan...

18:47.410 --> 18:49.640
Does it like its friend?

18:54.410 --> 18:56.020
Don't cry, Nanami.

18:57.410 --> 18:58.780
Ken-chan!

19:35.710 --> 19:45.410
Hisoka ni kitai suru kotoshi mo

19:35.710 --> 19:45.410
This year too, I'm secretly waiting

19:45.410 --> 19:52.460
Hachi tsuga izanaru

19:45.410 --> 19:52.460
August is waving to me

19:52.460 --> 20:02.410
Tsuyoki de tobikosu no tetora mo

19:52.460 --> 20:02.410
Tropical fish are jumping around energetically.

20:02.410 --> 20:11.660
Takanari ga yokan ni kawaru no

20:02.410 --> 20:11.660
My heart beat feels the premonition gradually

20:11.660 --> 20:18.810
Uchiyoseru nami hizashi semi no ote

20:11.660 --> 20:18.810
The leaping tide, along with sunshine, cicada's chirp

20:18.810 --> 20:24.360
Suashi yo terekusai kedo

20:18.810 --> 20:24.360
I feel a little embarrassed with my bare feet

20:24.360 --> 20:31.210
Kurikaesu natsu hanabi yoru fukashi

20:24.360 --> 20:31.210
Staying up late to see the fireworks every summer

20:31.210 --> 20:36.010
Dokidoki

20:31.210 --> 20:36.010
Makes me excited

20:36.010 --> 20:45.910
Shizumu yuuhi ni nami no ato ga

20:36.010 --> 20:45.910
In the sunset, the marks of the waves,

20:45.910 --> 20:52.610
Doko made mo tsuduku yo

20:45.910 --> 20:52.610
Stretch far.

20:52.610 --> 21:02.710
Jiguzagu shiroi sen oikake

20:52.610 --> 21:02.710
Chasing that white, zig-zag line

20:53.020 --> 20:54.910
Here you go, they're well iced.

20:54.940 --> 20:55.760
Thank you.

21:02.710 --> 21:13.510
Kono natsu wo uranau issho ka na? nante ne

21:02.710 --> 21:13.510
Can we spend this summer together?

21:02.710 --> 21:13.510


21:11.910 --> 21:12.640
Here.

21:21.710 --> 21:26.100
I didn't do it on purpose... for real.

21:26.410 --> 21:28.340
That's another favor you owe me, Ken-chan.

22:03.580 --> 22:06.460
For 50 years the world,

22:06.910 --> 22:09.760
under this oppression,

22:10.070 --> 22:13.810
has dreamed like the floating clouds.

22:14.510 --> 22:17.260
Stop with the idle talk! Everything will burn!

22:19.990 --> 22:21.800
Japan will perish.

22:22.340 --> 22:23.880
Why does the soldier keep protecting?

22:24.400 --> 22:26.340
Why are they trying to destroy Japan?

22:27.190 --> 22:28.250
Ken-chan!

22:28.920 --> 22:29.910
I'm coming in!

22:30.730 --> 22:32.570
You're playing games again?

22:32.750 --> 22:34.490
Don't say such things, Nanami-sensei!

22:34.770 --> 22:36.280
I am studying history!

22:36.520 --> 22:38.710
But you are dying again.

22:39.630 --> 22:42.000
Really all you do is play this.

22:42.200 --> 22:43.450
You owe me...!

22:42.470 --> 22:44.420
In short, first he beheads...

22:44.960 --> 22:46.950
Huh? The soldier ran into the bamboo!

22:47.590 --> 22:49.160
Ken-chan, are you listening?

22:58.320 --> 23:00.630
What are you doing!?

23:00.990 --> 23:02.940
Ken-chan is in the wrong!

23:03.620 --> 23:06.950
How many times must I tell you I'm studying history until you understand!?

23:07.350 --> 23:10.820
You say such things, but how many times must you let Japan perish!?

23:10.980 --> 23:14.110
The history has infinite possibilities!

23:13.720 --> 23:16.310
My, my, they are the same as always.

23:16.480 --> 23:19.220
Mmm, so it seems.

23:23.500 --> 23:24.320
Konoe-san.

23:24.890 --> 23:25.460
Yes?

23:29.330 --> 23:31.990
Umm, actually, I have something to say to you.

23:32.280 --> 23:34.070
Ah, what is it?

23:32.380 --> 23:37.380
